### 1. Get all bookings (empty [] before any are created) -> 200
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings


### 2. Create a valid booking -> 201 (and EV001 seats drop by 2)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### 3. Get one booking -> 200
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001


### 4. Create a booking with missing fields -> 400
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "",
  "participantName": "",
  "participantEmail": "",
  "seats": 0
}


### 5. Create a booking with an invalid event ID -> 404
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV999",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### 6. Create a booking with too many seats -> 400
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV002",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 100
}


### 7. Check seats reduced after booking -> EV001 availableSeats now 118
GET http://localhost:8081/api/events


### 8. Optional: cancel a booking -> 200, status CANCELLED, seats returned
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001
